xnu 0153: load the touch firmware, so the part can actually report

The part has no firmware of its own: the vendor driver writes an ISP stage and
five sections (223744 bytes) into it on every boot. Until it does, the IC info
block answers (length 193, config 0x46) but its misc fields read as zeros — so
touch_data_addr comes back as 0x1 and the "reports" the 0152 thread reads from
0x10308 are noise.

Read the package from a blob area in front of the log ring
(mondrian_ufs.c: mondrian_reserved_read; 256 KiB reserved, written once from
recovery with dd, no file system involved), then follow
goodix_brl_fwupdate.c for Berlin D: reset, hold the CPU (0x0002 = 01 00, read
0x2000 until three reads agree), misctl at 0xD804 = 0x20700000, watchdog off at
0xD040, ISP to 0x23800, eight 0x55 bytes at 0x10000, reset and check that
patch_pid[3..5] is "ISP", then each section in 4 KB packets (data plus a 32-bit
checksum to 0x12410, then a 0xBB command with its own checksum to 0x12400, ack
and status 0xEE).

The blob also carries the sensor config (1488 bytes, type 4 at 0x3e000), which
the vendor flashes before the five firmware sections; tools/mk-touch-blob.py
repacks it as table entry 1, so the kernel's table order matches. The update
resets use brl_reset's 2 ms low pulse, not brl_power_on's 15 ms one.

The IC info's parm block is variable length (five count bytes, each followed by
that many u16 values), so misc is not at a fixed offset. Parse the counts the
way convert_ic_info does and read misc.touch_data_addr/head_len/point_len from
the right place; only start the report thread for a sane address, or the thread
reads a stale block and feeds backboardd noise. After the IC info, send
brl_set_coor_mode's commands (0x90/0 rawdata off, 0x91/0x81 coordinates on) to
misc.cmd_addr; without them the touch block returns rawdata, not points. The
update's final reset is 2 ms (brl_reset); do brl_power_on's 15 ms reset once
after it, as the vendor's resume does, before reading the IC info and enabling
coordinates, or the part stays in the post-update rawdata state. After that
reset, repeat brl_dev_confirm's eight 0xAA bytes at 0x10000: the vendor's
power-on does it before the IC info and the coordinate mode.
mondriantouch=0 skips the whole driver for UI-only boots; mondriantouchpoll=1
makes the report thread read the block regardless of the IRQ pin, for bring-up.

The loader also prints patch_vid, sensor_id and the config ID at 0x10076, so
one boot log says whether the part is running the firmware or still the ROM.

